{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task is AGENT-TF-01: implement `api_call_loss_filter` through `solve(case)`.\n\nFrom the candidate artifact description:\n1. For each call: subtract loss_with_call from loss_without_call to get gain\n2. Normalize gain by prediction_tokens (at least one)\n3. Require both parseability AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n4. Keep diagnostics in supplied call order\n5. Return accepted call IDs and per-call diagnostics\n\nLet me work through the logic:\n\nFor each call:\n- gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call\n- normalized_gain = gain / max(prediction_tokens, 1)  (normalize by at least one token)\n- accepted = parseable AND (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n\nThe output:\n- diagnostics: list of {call_id, accepted, normalized_gain} in input order\n- accepted_call_ids: list of call_ids where accepted=True\n\nLet me verify with case 0:\n- threshold = 0.05\n- call0: gain = 1.48911432 - 0.30132987 = 1.18778445, norm_gain = 1.18778445/5 = 0.23755689, parseable=true → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.37006381 - 0.10127803 = 1.26878578, norm_gain = 1.26878578/5 = 0.25375716, parseable=true → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.07992348 - 0.04054692 = 1.03937656, norm_gain = 1.03937656/5 = 0.20787531, parseable=true → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.76582941 - 0.57732788 = 1.18850153, norm_gain = 1.18850153/3 = 0.39616718, parseable=true → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.70674574 - 0.40289862 = 1.30384712, norm_gain = 1.30384712/6 = 0.21730785, parseable=true → accepted\n- call5: gain = 1.98682122 - 0.89260518 = 1.09421604, norm_gain = 1.09421604/4 = 0.27355401, parseable=false → NOT accepted\n\nSo accepted_call_ids = [\"call0\", \"call1\", \"call2\", \"call3\", \"call4\"]\n\nThe description mentions \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - I need to think about how to round. It says \"rounded\" but doesn't specify precision. Let me not round or maybe round to a reasonable number of decimals. Actually, re-reading: \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" - but the schema says normalized_gain is type \"number\" with no rounding specification. I'll leave as float without explicit rounding, or maybe round to some reasonable precision. Let me just keep the float as is and not round explicitly, since no precision is given.\n\nNow let me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        # Validate required fields\n        for field in [\"call_id\", \"loss_without_call\", \"loss_with_call\", \"prediction_tokens\", \"parseable\"]:\n            if field not in call:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Missing required field: {field}\")\n        \n        # Normalize by at least one prediction token\n        tokens = max(prediction_tokens, 1)\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\n        \n        # Require both parseability and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Let me also add validation for the case payload itself.\n\nThe response must be a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string. No markdown, no extra text.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate top-level fields\\n    if \\\"threshold\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field: threshold\\\")\\n    if \\\"calls\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field: calls\\\")\\n\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        # Validate required call fields\\n        for field in (\\\"call_id\\\", \\\"loss_without_call\\\", \\\"loss_with_call\\\", \\\"prediction_tokens\\\", \\\"parseable\\\"):\\n            if field not in call:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Call missing required field: {field}\\\")\\n\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        # Normalize gain by at least one prediction token (stronger counterfactual)\\n        tokens = max(prediction_tokens, 1)\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\\n\\n        # Inclusive threshold: accept if parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\\n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01K6v1PWNevtNcvR9qyIm8p1","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2430},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2430,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":82,"output_tokens":1544,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1090},"service_tier":"standard"}}